            <ArticleTitle>Claudication on mastication following bilateral external carotid ligation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ligation of both external carotid arteries to control epistaxis can produce a decrease in the blood supply of the muscles of mastication sufficient to cause pain typical of claudication while chewing. We report 3 cases of this complication. We advocate that this procedure be used only in special circumstances.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
